in authored/evidence-status.json.","citation_ids":["cite.long.thm-tr-finite-decision"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.thm-tr-finite-decision"],"id":"long.thm-tr-finite-decision","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Theorem 8.9 (Finite decision procedure)","locator":"Long record Theorem 8.9, p. 96, label thm:tr-finite-decision","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*Call $n\\in[4,L_J/2]$ **bad** if no $M\\in[n,2n-2]$ has $\\mu_J(M)\\le\\tfrac{11}{15}$, and set $B(J):=\\max(\\mathrm{bad}\\cup\\{3\\})$. Then $\\mathrm{HalfRung}(J)$ holds iff the greedy orbit for $1/2$ under weights $w_n^{(J)}$ survives every rank from $2$ through $B(J)$. This is a finite exact decision procedure.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/long.thm-tr-finite-decision","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/long.thm-tr-finite-decision","id":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/edges/%5B%22long.thm-tr-finite-decision%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_rung_finite_decision%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/edges/%5B%22long.thm-tr-finite-decision%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_rung_finite_decision%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_rung_finite_decision"},{"derived":true,"family":"provenance","from":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/edges/%5B%22long.thm-tr-finite-decision%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_rung_finite_decision%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","id":"field:70c720799c8900415c3b60361a93be4a73285dab702aba169